title: sync panel
tags: Panel
kind: reference
summary: Synchronises two repositories: pick the pair, read their status, compute and review a plan, resolve its conflicts, run it.

Open it with `panel:open here sync` (<<key "panel:open here sync" "t y">>). It drives
the same sync engine as `mf sync`, so nothing here needs a shell ([[Sync]],
[[Syncing two repositories]]).

The toolbar picks repository ''A'' (the active one by default) and ''B'' (another
loaded one; never the same as A), and takes the path of the intents file the plan
is computed from. Then, in order:

* ''Status'' (<<key "sync:status" "Ctrl+r">>) — the links between the two repositories, one row per link with its state.
* ''Plan'' (<<key "sync:plan" "p o">>) — computes the plan from the intents file: its number of operations and its warnings, then the overlay and the conflicts below.
* ''Show'' (<<key "sync:open" "p Shift+o">>) — the overlay of the current plan: its operations counted by kind, and in red each one the run would skip because its record changed since planning (green when every baseline is still current). Then the conflicts.
* ''Run'' (<<key "sync:run" "p p">>) — runs the plan, after a confirmation, and reports what was done and skipped, the subtrees diverging from an external tool, and the warnings.

Status and Plan also say what they found on the status bar, and Run what it did.

<<key "view:refresh self" "Ctrl+r">> reads the loaded repositories again, keeping the pair,
then what the view shows: the status after Status or Run, the stored plan after Plan
or Show ([[Generic panel commands]]). It never plans or runs: both write.

!! From the command input, or a script

Every step is a command, so a sync runs without the toolbar ([[mf gui command]]):
`sync:pair A B` chooses the two repositories (by name or uuid; an unknown one, or the
same one twice, is refused), and `sync:plan [intents]` takes the intents file as its
argument, filling the toolbar's field with it. A step without a pair, or a plan without
an intents file, is refused rather than ignored.

Show and Run need a plan for the pair. The panel never asks during a plan: its
conflicts are left skipped. A conflict row shows the field and its value on each
side; choose `skip`, `a` or `b` and ''Save'' to record the resolution in the plan,
for the run to apply ([[Sync conflicts]]).
